                    {
                        "sense_id": "bfe24feb-52fe-34b5-944b-8c7dec4b7c06",
                        "entry_id": "e360e5a0-fb92-37ad-b1aa-c4307d7e8ba9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Nom de plusieurs marsupiaux de la famille des Dasyuridae, souvent appelées souris marsupiales, endémiques d’Australie, et pour deux ou trois espèces, de Nouvelle-Guinée."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c7af4273-a196-4b99-ad65-1ddb032008ec",
                                "sense_id": "bfe24feb-52fe-34b5-944b-8c7dec4b7c06",
                                "text": "Les effectifs d’un autre petit marsupial endémique, l’antechine fauve (Antechinus bellus), qui vit dans le nord de l’Australie, ont chuté de plus de 30 % en moins de dix ans."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2cae197c-abd3-4a7d-b037-20f85625b375",
                        "source_entry_id": "e360e5a0-fb92-37ad-b1aa-c4307d7e8ba9",
                        "source_sense_id": "bfe24feb-52fe-34b5-944b-8c7dec4b7c06",
                        "target_lang_word": "Breitfuß-Beutelmaus",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "81719018-ccfc-419e-b0a2-408c3c5ee856",
                        "source_entry_id": "e360e5a0-fb92-37ad-b1aa-c4307d7e8ba9",
                        "source_sense_id": "bfe24feb-52fe-34b5-944b-8c7dec4b7c06",
                        "target_lang_word": "antechinus",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "antechinus",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a16a2417-fa2e-37a8-82ef-ca57b7d86a35",
                                        "entry_id": "04645d53-c492-3cd1-b512-a5adff1f2c86",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any member of the genus Antechinus of small carnivorous marsupials that resemble shrews."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "018253ef-85c7-4000-95b1-c397a7602982",
                                                "sense_id": "a16a2417-fa2e-37a8-82ef-ca57b7d86a35",
                                                "text": "These are distinguished from the Monodelphia, or Placentalia, by bringing forth their young in a very rudimentary state, nourishing them in a “marsupium,” which is either a regular pouch or a simple skinfold, such as our native cats and antechini develop at the time of parturition."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9a476de3-ae49-4c7b-a283-22215f7acb9c",
                                                "sense_id": "a16a2417-fa2e-37a8-82ef-ca57b7d86a35",
                                                "text": "Being on the West Coast at the time, and always anxious to forward any scientific investigations, I collected all the varieties of kangaroo rats, antechini, and rats that came under my observation."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ae41cd3e-98dd-4858-9722-b3491b49f531",
                                                "sense_id": "a16a2417-fa2e-37a8-82ef-ca57b7d86a35",
                                                "text": "Smaller than the wambengers, the antechinuses are secretive and are seldom seen by people unless they are caught and brought into houses by domestic cats."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dee6ef86-9921-4cee-87c6-24bb913b469c",
                                                "sense_id": "a16a2417-fa2e-37a8-82ef-ca57b7d86a35",
                                                "text": "Two species of antechini live above the snowline. These are pugnacious rat-sized marsupials. Male antechini copulate so vigorously that they die from exhaustion."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "478785cc-1db4-4166-8ef9-645b6f84c0ef",
                                                "sense_id": "a16a2417-fa2e-37a8-82ef-ca57b7d86a35",
                                                "text": "I thought it was my fault until I consulted the experts, and found that antechinus die naturally at this time of the year.[…]Antechinus eat beetles, spiders and cockroaches, which they find in decaying litter and topsoil in their habitat of dense ground cover."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f95c4dab-a781-4600-a018-af53bdfad3de",
                                                "sense_id": "a16a2417-fa2e-37a8-82ef-ca57b7d86a35",
                                                "text": "If held as a colony outside the breeding season, antechinus show relatively little aggression while still forming a linear hierarchy."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
